WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.642
Real analysis often requires information stored in more than one table.

00:00:04.642 --> 00:00:12.347
An orders table may contain customer I D, while a separate customers table contains the customer segment.

00:00:12.347 --> 00:00:17.182
A merge combines those related tables using a shared key.

00:00:17.182 --> 00:00:24.492
The example performs a left merge so all orders remain in the result and customer information is added when a matching

00:00:24.492 --> 00:00:32.132
customer exists. The validation option checks the expected relationship between the tables.

00:00:32.685 --> 00:00:36.457
Never assume a merge is correct just because it runs.

00:00:36.457 --> 00:00:42.037
Check the row count before and after the merge, inspect unmatched keys,

00:00:42.037 --> 00:00:47.937
and think about whether the relationship should be one-to-one, one-to-many, or many-to-many.

00:00:47.937 --> 00:00:51.252
Incorrect joins can silently duplicate data.
